{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he shall not have a portion in the midst of his brothers.</b> In the Sifrei they expounded: 'ונחלה לא יהיה לו' — this is the portion of the rest. That means those who were not brothers to Levi except from his father's side, such as Yosef, Dan, Naftali, Gad, Asher, and Binyamin. 'בקרב אחיו' — this is the portion of the five, those who were his brothers both from his father's side and from his mother's side, such as Reuven, Shimon, Yehuda, Yissakhar, Zevulun. And both exclusions are necessary, for if only one exclusion were written, we would establish it regarding the portion of his brothers who were his brothers from his father's side but not from his mother's side — but regarding the portion of his brothers from his father's side and his mother's side, I might say he would inherit among them. Therefore two exclusions are stated. Another interpretation: 'portion of the rest' means the rest of the tribes, whom Moshe and Yehoshua did not give as an inheritance. 'Portion of the five' means the five tribes whom Moshe and Yehoshua gave as an inheritance. For this is what happened: Moshe gave an inheritance to the Reuveni, the Gadi, and half the tribe of Menasheh. And Yehoshua gave an inheritance to Yehuda, Efrayim, and half the tribe of Menasheh."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:15.940338507Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}